Following up on our call, I want to put the Lenders' current position in writ=
ing so we can move toward documentation.

In light of the currently contemplated Transaction, and without in any way co=
nstituting a waiver until definitive documentation is executed, the Required =
Lenders are prepared to consent to an amendment addressing Section 8.08 (Chan=
ge of Control Under This Agreement) of the Credit Agreement (credit_agreement=
.pdf) on the following basis:

(a) Repayment of drawn balances. The Lenders require that any Revolving Loans=
 outstanding under the Credit Agreement be repaid in full at or prior to the =
closing of the Transaction, rather than assumed by the surviving borrower. We=
 understand your preference is to assume the facility undrawn and simply re-a=
ffirm the Loan Parties post-closing; we are not in a position to agree to tha=
t without a compensating adjustment elsewhere, for the reasons below.

(b) Conditioned waiver, not an unconditional one. On our call you asked wheth=
er the Change of Control waiver could be unconditional. The Lenders' position=
 is that it cannot be: we are prepared to waive the Section 8.08 Change of Co=
ntrol default, but only conditioned on delivery, at closing, of an updated Co=
mpliance Certificate demonstrating pro forma compliance with Section 6.01 (Ma=
ximum Total Net Leverage Ratio) after giving effect to the Transaction and an=
y new indebtedness incurred in connection with it. An unconditioned waiver wo=
uld leave the Lenders exposed to a leverage profile they have not had the opp=
ortunity to underwrite.

(c) Amendment fee. The Lenders require an amendment fee, payable at closing, =
in the amount customary for a Change of Control consent of this type; we will=
 circulate a specific proposal once the above is agreed in principle.

(d) Information. We will also need updated financial statements and a pro for=
ma leverage build reflecting the Transaction before the Required Lenders will=
 sign off, consistent with the reporting covenant already in the Credit Agree=
ment.

We recognize this is more conditionality than you were hoping for, and we are=
 open to discussing the sequencing - for example, whether the compliance rech=
eck could be satisfied by a bring-down certificate delivered a short period a=
fter closing rather than literally at closing, if that is the sticking point.=
 But an unconditional waiver combined with an assumed, undrawn facility is no=
t something we can bring to the Required Lenders as currently structured.

Please let us know a good time this week to continue the discussion. We would=
 like to have documentation substantially agreed well ahead of any signing.

